From 9bb9d87b80fa9c295f6d9d05455ff37a68c4f0ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:16:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] feat(add): doMerge=false installs, pinned refs, registry
 and macroEngine

Completes the config command and the version-pinned install flow, and
integrates the macroEngine datapack.

config (was an empty stub):
  sculk config                       show every value
  sculk config doMerge true|false    merge vs. separate-pack installs
  sculk config author <name>         default author for new libraries.json
  sculk config initTemplate <name>
  sculk config list | reset | help
`sculk init` and `sculk makelib` now stamp the configured author instead of
the OS username.

separate installs (doMerge=false):
  A library is laid down as its own pack next to the project, which is what
  Minecraft loads as a separate datapack. Resourcepack libraries are
  redirected to the sibling resourcepacks/ folder. If the project is not
  inside a datapacks/ or resourcepacks/ folder, sculk refuses to write into
  the parent directory (which could be anywhere on disk) and installs under
  <project>/libraries/<id> with a warning instead.

registry:
  Adds uuid, astar, playermotion, titlewriter, speclib, reef, hitmatch,
  stringlib and macroengine/macroengine-rp, each with a description, author
  and pack kind. Entries may declare a Subdir so a library can live inside a
  monorepo. `sculk list [--json] [--installed] [filter]` renders the same
  table the website is generated from.

macroEngine:
  Registered from IronCrest-sudo/core at archived/macroEngine-Datapack-v26.4
  (string, cooldown, multi-cmd, math, nbt, geo, hooks, permissions, uuid
  cache, input system) plus its companion resource pack. The pack ships no
  libraries.json, so sculk synthesizes one from the upstream archive
  registry (v26.4-snapshot-1, format 122) and surfaces the archive notice
  and load-gate instructions.

version handling:
  Game version compatibility is now a constraint check instead of string
  equality, so a library may declare ">=26.2" or "<1.20.1". Tag merging
  de-duplicates values so re-installing does not grow load.json. An unknown
  game version in `sculk init` falls back to the closest known layout rather
  than producing an empty project.

Ref separators:
  git stores refs as files, so a repo cannot hold both refs/heads/1.0.0 and
  refs/heads/1.0.0/26.2. sculk accepts "/", "+" and "_" as the
  version/game-version separator so both layouts are publishable; "-" is
  excluded because game versions contain one ("26.4-snapshot-1"). A test
  pins this git limitation so the workaround cannot be removed by accident.

Also implements `sculk install` (was an empty stub) honouring the recorded
ref and install mode, makes `sculk update`/`uninstall`/`remove` return
errors, and fixes the uninstall log claiming to have deleted blacklisted
files it skipped.
