From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:36:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] feat(web): libraries page, API server and real showcase
 recordings

Completes the two remaining Goals from the roadmap: a website where Sculk
users can find available libraries, and showcase media.

website:
  - /libraries renders the registry generated from the CLI itself
    (`sculk list --json > website/src/data/libraries.json`), so the site can
    never drift from what `sculk add` accepts. It offers live filtering,
    copyable install commands, per-library repo/path/notice info, and an
    install guide for both merge and separate-pack modes.
  - If a sculk API server is reachable on the same origin the page refreshes
    itself from /api/libraries and notes how many entries are newer than the
    build; without a server the static data stays on screen.
  - The empty showcase slots on the index page now hold real recordings.

server:
  - GET /api/libraries[?q=&kind=] and /api/libraries/:id serve the same
    generated registry, with CORS so a separately hosted site can use it.
  - The previously invalid version.ts is now a real /api/version endpoint,
    and app.ts registers the routes, binds 0.0.0.0 and answers JSON 404s.
  - Added tsconfig + typecheck/dev/start scripts; dotenv moved to runtime deps.

showcase (real, not mocked):
  - tools/record-showcase.sh runs the actual sculk binary in a throwaway
    world and records three sessions with asciinema.
  - tools/cast2gif.py renders the casts to animated GIFs with Pillow, pulling
    colour emoji straight out of NotoColorEmoji's CBDT table, stripping log
    timestamps, preserving real pacing and capping frame sizes.
  - GIFs land in website/public/showcase/ and are embedded in Showcase.astro.

Rerunning `website/tools/record-showcase.sh all` reproduces all three GIFs.
